# Metro — a Rails- and Phoenix-like web framework for Kex.
#
# Pages are rendered on the server and kept live over a WebSocket; forms are
# checked by declared validations; sign-in rests on hashed passwords and
# server-side sessions.
#
#   Metro.Live.Socket    one live page's WebSocket: state, step, render
#   Metro.Live.Hub       tells a user's other tabs their page is stale
#   Metro.Live.Client    the browser script, and the route that serves it
#   Metro.Validation     `validates(…)` rules, checked into a changeset
#   Metro.Auth.Password  PBKDF2 password hashes
#   Metro.Auth.Token     session tokens, stored as digests
#   Metro.Cookies        reading and issuing cookies, same-origin test
#   Metro.Plugs          the same-origin plug
#   Metro.Decimal        decimals as scaled integers
#   Metro.Environment    METRO_ENV, PORT and HOST: where the process runs
#   Metro.Clock          the time as seconds, milliseconds or microseconds
#   Metro.Id             ids for rows, and serial numbers for tabs
#   Metro.TimeZones      the names of the world's time zones
#
# Requests are routed by `Metro.Router`, on Kex's `Net.HTTP`. README.md is
# the guide.
module Metro do
  export Metro.Live.Socket
  export Metro.Live.Hub
  export Metro.Live.Client
  export Metro.Validation
  export Metro.Auth.Password
  export Metro.Auth.Token
  export Metro.Cookies
  export Metro.Plugs
  export Metro.Decimal
  export Metro.Environment
  export Metro.Clock
  export Metro.Id
  export Metro.TimeZones
end
